# The named character references of the HTML Living Standard, 2,231 names,
# each to the one or two code points it stands for. `refs.hero` reads them.
#
# Generated, never edited by hand: the Heroes program
# `rebel/generators/html_entities/` read the standard's `entities.json`, kept
# in its folder `whatwg/` as html.spec.whatwg.org served it on 2026-11-22
# (SHA-256 d741d877ac77c4194c4ad526b5b4a19aef8dfe411ab840a466891cdbb9f362e6),
# sorted its names by their bytes and wrote this module whole; its `check`
# command says whether this module is still what it writes.
#
# `NAMES[i]` is written as the table writes it, `&` left off: `amp;`, and the
# old `amp` that the standard reads without its `;`. `POINTS[i]` holds its
# characters as `first << 21 | second`, `second` 0 where there is one.

# Every name, in the order of its bytes.
constant NAMES: [str]
